{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310816,"nonce":"z6/gST6XANuo8NlVHT5LLYs9njw=","title":"RESOLVED (commit 97398cc). The residual wasm per-token leak (~390 KB/token, capped long-gen at ~3300 tokens after GGUF-buffer free 496f1f2) ...","message":"**RESOLVED 2026-06-15 (commit 97398cc).** Onset pushed from ~3300 to\neffectively unbounded; forced 3600-tok wasm gen clean ([done] timing\ncorrect, peak RSS 1.96 GB, 0 STRCONCAT_OVF). Two latent runtime bugs were\nworked around — documented in [[bugs_wasm_anon_struct_and_blit]]. Original\nattribution + plan kept below for reference.\n\n\n**Attribution (2026-06-15, global-allocator histogram + per-entry counters in\nruntime-wasm, all reverted):** after 496f1f2 (free GGUF file buffer) the wasm\nheap is ~0.9 GB weight base + **~390 KB/token leak**. The leak is **STRINGS**,\nnot arrays/anon/boxes:\n- `alloc_string_data` calls = **~50% of all allocations**, split EXACTLY between\n  `haxe_string_concat_sret` (+444k / 2M allocs) and `haxe_string_substring`\n  (+444k / 2M allocs) — paired 1:1. `haxe_array_new`, `haxe_anon_new`,\n  `haxe_box_*`, `haxe_string_from_bytes` all FLAT (load-only). The leaked bytes\n  are the \u003c=64 B size class (live-by-bucket), ~50 B each.\n- **Bisect:** skipping `decodeBuffer(rawPieces)` per token = NO change (still\n  444k). Skipping the `rawPieces += piece` accumulation (made it non-growing) =\n  alloc count COLLAPSES (doesn't reach 2M in 250 tok). So the source is the\n  **growing-String accumulation**, not the re-decode. (The exact per-call\n  mechanism for why one `+=` of a growing String shows as thousands of\n  concat+substring/token was not nailed — likely the wasm String `+=` lowering\n  copies via substring+concat — but the bisect is decisive on WHICH line.)\n- Determinism: LocalTempSampler uses a fixed seed, so two runs are byte-identical\n  → A/B counter comparisons are valid even at temp 0.7.\n\n**Root:** `GenerationLoop.generate` keeps `var rawPieces = \"\";` and does\n`rawPieces += decodePiece(id)` every token (growing String), then\n`decodeBuffer(rawPieces)` re-decodes the FULL buffer to hand the callback\n`partial` (full text so far). On wasm there is no amortized append\n(`StringBuf` is broken — [[bugs_wasm_generic_string_concat]]), so the growing\nString is O(N) per token = **O(N^2)** and the dominant per-token leak. This is\nthe \"O(N^2) decode\" the 2ea4de0 note only partially mitigated.\n\n**THE FIX (clean — all callers ready):** every `generate()` caller already does\n`delta = partial.substr(prevLen); prevLen = partial.length` (llama-chat\nMain.hx:355; llama-chat-server Main.hx:276 + :289) — they ONLY use the delta.\nSo change the `onToken` contract from `partial` (full text) to `delta` (new\ntext):\n1. `GenerationLoop`: drop the growing `rawPieces` String. Keep a small\n   `carry:String` (\u003c=3 byte-alphabet chars = an incomplete trailing UTF-8\n   codepoint). Per token: `combined = carry + decodePiece(id)`;\n   `tailLen = incompleteUtf8TailLen(combined)`;\n   `delta = byteDecode(combined.substr(0, combined.length - tailLen))`;\n   `carry = combined.substr(combined.length - tailLen)`; `onToken(id, delta)`.\n   All O(1)/token, no growing String.\n2. For the return value (`prompt + full text`): push deltas into an\n   `Array\u003cString\u003e` (O(1) amortized) and `join(\"\")` ONCE at the end.\n3. `incompleteUtf8TailLen(s)`: map the trailing byte-alphabet chars to raw bytes\n   via `byteDecoderArray()`; from the end, if the last raw byte is a lead byte\n   needing more continuations than present, the codepoint is incomplete → return\n   its length (1-3); else 0. (Codepoints are \u003c=4 bytes = \u003c=4 byte-alphabet\n   chars, so the carry stays tiny.)\n4. Update the 3 callers to use `delta` directly (delete the substr/prevLen\n   dance) + the `generate` doc (partial → delta).\n\n**VERIFY:** byte-identical streamed output (deterministic seed) before/after on\na long run + the per-50-token fmt(123.456) tripwire staying clean WELL past 3300\ntokens (the leak should drop from ~390 KB/token toward ~0, pushing onset toward\nunbounded). Re-attribute with the runtime-wasm counters to confirm\nconcat+substring flatten. cargo fmt/clippy not needed (Haxe-only change).\n\n**Risk:** the incremental UTF-8 carry is the only subtle part — a wrong boundary\nsilently corrupts multi-byte codepoints at token boundaries. Verify against the\nold full-buffer `byteDecode` output byte-for-byte. Deferred to a focused session\nrather than rushed; the corruption itself is already fixed (496f1f2, onset\n~3300), so this is robustness for \u003e3300-token generations, not a crash fix.\n\n**Alternative:** fix `StringBuf` on wasm (the generic-string-concat compiler\nbug) — then the growing buffer becomes amortized O(1) and NO contract change is\nneeded. Broader fix, helps all wasm string-building, but a harder compiler change\nthan the nue-side delta contract.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `perf_wasm_decode_loop_onsquared_strings` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}